{
 "cells": [
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "## CG test for $[2,1,0]\\otimes[2,1,0]$: does $\\langle v_{\\rm new}|\\otimes\\langle\\mathrm{HWS}|$ give a basis after untwisting?\n\nWrite-up: `xxx-210-cg-test.tex` / `.pdf`. From `L2-mathcalA.wb` (adjoint): $\\langle k_1^{u/h}Q_1\\rangle\\langle k_2^{u/h}Q_{12}\\rangle_m=\\big(\\langle v_{\\rm tot}|\\otimes\\langle\\mathrm{vacL}|\\big)|\\Psi_A\\rangle$ with\n$$\\langle v_{\\rm tot}|=\\langle v_1|\\big(1-k_2\\,\\hat t(\\theta_1)\\big),\\quad \\langle v_1|=(1-k_1z_1)\\,e_1^Te^{p_1'E_{12}}e^{p_2E_{13}}e^{p_3E_{23}},\\quad \\hat t=\\frac{t^{(1)}_2(\\theta_1)}{\\nu_1^{(1)}(\\theta_1)\\nu_1^{(1)}(\\theta_1-h)}.$$\n$\\langle\\mathrm{vacL}|=e_1^T g_0$, $g_0=e^{p_1E_{12}}e^{p_2E_{13}}e^{p_3E_{23}}$. Undo it with the **global** rotation $g_0^{-1}\\otimes g_0^{-1}$: $\\big(\\langle v_{\\rm tot}|\\otimes\\langle\\mathrm{vacL}|\\big)(g_0^{-1}\\otimes g_0^{-1})=\\langle v_{\\rm new}|\\otimes e_1^T$, $\\ \\langle v_{\\rm new}|=\\langle v_{\\rm tot}|g_0^{-1}$. Then untwist, $z_k=e^{\\varphi_k\\varepsilon}$, take the leading order in $\\varepsilon$ **separately in each weight space** of $V$ (the global leading order $\\varepsilon^0$ is only $\\tfrac12(1-k_1)(2-k_2)\\,e_1^T$), and count ranks of the coefficient vectors in the free parameters $(k_1,k_2,p_1,p_2,\\varphi,\\theta_1,h)$.\n\n**Results** (exact, symbolic; cells 3–7)\n- $v_1g_0^{-1}=(1-k_1z_1)\\,e_1^Te^{(p_1'-p_1)E_{12}}$ with $p_1'-p_1=O(\\varepsilon)$.\n- Weight spaces of $V$: leading orders $\\varepsilon^0$ at $(2,1,0)$, $\\varepsilon^1$ at $(2,0,1),(1,2,0)$, $\\varepsilon^2$ at $(1,1,1)$ (rank **2** = dim), $\\varepsilon^3$ at $(0,2,1)$. The components at $(1,0,2)$ and $(0,1,2)$ are **identically zero**, already at finite twist. So 6 of 8.\n- $V\\otimes V$: covectors $c\\otimes e_1^T$ reach 6 of 64 states.\n- **Highest-weight states of $V\\otimes V$: 5 of 6.** $[4,2,0]$, $[3,3,0]$, $[4,1,1]$ and both copies of $[3,2,1]$ are reached; the **singlet $[2,2,2]$ is missed**, because it pairs only with the site-1 lowest weight $(0,1,2)$, where $v_{\\rm new}=0$.\n- Parameter dependence (cell 6): $k_1,k_2$ survive the limit; $\\theta_1,h$ drop out. In each 1-dim weight space all parameters are overall factors (several components exist only because of $k_1$ or $k_2$). In the octet sector the vector is $-\\tfrac12k_2p_2(\\varphi_1-\\varphi_2)(\\varphi_1-\\varphi_3)\\,(2k_1-1,\\,1)$: **$k_1$ alone** gives rank 2 and separates the two octets (freezing $k_1$ gives rank 1; freezing everything else keeps rank 2).\n- Where the lower weights come from (cell 7, exact): $v_1g_0^{-1}\\propto e_1^Te^{aE_{12}}$ lives only in the weights $(2,1,0),(1,2,0)$, and with a diagonal twist $\\hat t$ commutes with the Cartan, so it would stay there. In $v_{\\rm new}=v_1g_0^{-1}\\big(1-k_2\\,g_0\\hat tg_0^{-1}\\big)$ the conjugation gives $\\hat t^{G_1}$ with the rotated twist $G_1=g_0Gg_0^{-1}$ (covariance and quantum Cauchy–Binet verified). $G_1$ is upper triangular with $(G_1)_{12}=p_1(z_2-z_1)$, $(G_1)_{23}=p_2(z_1-z_3)/p_1$, both $O(\\varepsilon)$, and $(G_1)_{13}=0$ (fixed by the vacL relation for $p_3$).\n\n**Later sections.**\n- Cells 8–10: the determinant family $v'_{\\rm new}$ reaches 3/6 hw states, and the combined total is still 5/6.\n- Cells 11–13: the transfer-matrix family $\\langle\\mathrm{vacL}\\otimes\\mathrm{vacL}|t_{\\{2,1\\}}(\\theta_1)\\to v_t=e_1^TG^{-1}g_0Gg_0^{-1}$ reaches 4/6 alone and nothing new.\n- Cells 14–15: **why** the rule $\\nu_3\\le\\lambda_2$ holds. For the $\\hat t$ families it is at most one slot-3 unit per quantum minor, whatever the twist. For $v_t$ it is the zero $(1,3)$ entry. The hypothetical $v^{(2)}=e_1^TG^{-2}g_0G^2g_0^{-1}$ reaches the singlet (6/6), but it is not $t_{\\{2,1\\}}(\\theta_1)^2$.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "ps[rep_] :=\n    ps[rep] =\n    Block[\n        {res = (Prepend[rep, #]& /@ (Tuples[Table[Range[rep〚1, i + 1〛, rep〚1, i〛], {i, 1, Length[rep〚1〛] - 1}]]))},\n        If[Length[res〚1, 1〛] == 1, Reverse @ Sort @ res, Reverse @ Sort @ Flatten[ps /@ res, 1]]\n    ];\ndim[rep_] := dim[rep] = Length[ps[{rep}]];\nJ0[k_][pat_] := J0[k][pat] = Sum[pat〚k, i〛, {i, 1, k}] - Sum[pat〚k - 1, i〛, {i, 1, k - 1}];\nJp[k_][pat_] :=\n    Jp[k][pat] =\n    -Sum[\n        Product[pat〚k, i〛 - i - pat〚k + 1, j〛 + j, {j, Range[k + 1]}]\n        / Product[pat〚k, i〛 - i - pat〚k, j〛 + j, {j, Complement[Range[k], {i}]}] v[ReplacePart[pat, {k, i} → pat〚k, i〛 + 1]],\n        {i, 1, k}\n    ];\nJm[k_][pat_] :=\n    Jm[k][pat] =\n    Sum[\n        Product[pat〚k, i〛 - i - pat〚k - 1, j〛 + j, {j, Range[k - 1]}]\n        / Product[pat〚k, i〛 - i - pat〚k, j〛 + j, {j, Complement[Range[k], {i}]}] v[ReplacePart[pat, {k, i} → pat〚k, i〛 - 1]],\n        {i, 1, k}\n    ];\nJJ[k_, l_, rep_] :=\n    JJ[k, l, rep] =\n    Which[\n        k == l,\n        DiagonalMatrix[J0[k] /@ ps[{rep}]],\n        l == k + 1,\n        Transpose[Table[Coefficient[Jp[k][ps[{rep}]〚i〛], v[#]]& /@ ps[{rep}], {i, 1, Length[ps[{rep}]]}]],\n        l == k - 1,\n        Transpose[Table[Coefficient[Jm[l][ps[{rep}]〚i〛], v[#]]& /@ ps[{rep}], {i, 1, Length[ps[{rep}]]}]],\n        l > k + 1,\n        JJ[k, k + 1, rep].JJ[k + 1, l, rep] - JJ[k + 1, l, rep].JJ[k, k + 1, rep],\n        l < k - 1,\n        JJ[k, k - 1, rep].JJ[k - 1, l, rep] - JJ[k - 1, l, rep].JJ[k, k - 1, rep]\n    ];",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "(* ---- 1. Single site (site 1), L1-mathcalA conventions, everything exact with symbolic z[k], θ[1], h, p1, p2, k1, k2.\n   T_ij(u) = (u - θ1) δ_ij - h E_ji, t_a = sum_{|I|=a} z_I qminor_{I,I}, t-hat = t_2(θ1)/(ν1(θ1) ν1(θ1 - h)).\n   v_new = v_tot . g0^-1 is the site-1 covector left after undoing the global rotation, site 2 becoming e1^T. ---- *)\nClearAll[lamC, dC, EC, LaxC, qminC, tGC, nu1C, p3C, g0C, p1pC, v1C, tHatC, vtotC, vnewC];\nlamC = {2, 1, 0}; dC = dim[lamC];\nEC[i_, j_] := EC[i, j] = JJ[i, j, lamC];\nLaxC[i_, j_][x_] := (x - θ[1]) KroneckerDelta[i, j] IdentityMatrix[dC] - h EC[j, i];\nqminC[II_][x_] := Sum[Signature[s] Dot @@ Table[LaxC[II[[s[[k]]]], II[[k]]][x - (k - 1) h], {k, Length[II]}], {s, Permutations[Range[Length[II]]]}];\ntGC[a_][x_] := Sum[(Times @@ (z /@ II)) qminC[II][x], {II, Subsets[Range[3], {a}]}];\nnu1C[x_] := x - θ[1] - h lamC[[1]];\n\np3C = p2 (z[3] - z[1]) / (p1 (z[2] - z[3]));\ng0C = MatrixExp[p1 EC[1, 2]] . MatrixExp[p2 EC[1, 3]] . MatrixExp[p3C EC[2, 3]];\np1pC = p1 (1 - k1 z[2]) / (1 - k1 z[1]);\nv1C = (1 - k1 z[1])^(lamC[[1]] - lamC[[2]]) UnitVector[dC, 1] . MatrixExp[p1pC EC[1, 2]] . MatrixExp[p2 EC[1, 3]] . MatrixExp[p3C EC[2, 3]];\ntHatC = Together[tGC[2][θ[1]] / (nu1C[θ[1]] nu1C[θ[1] - h])];\nvtotC = v1C . (IdentityMatrix[dC] - k2 tHatC);\nvnewC = Together /@ (vtotC . Inverse[g0C]);\n\nGrid[\n    {\n        {\"E_ij (i<j) raise: e1 is annihilated by E12, E13, E23\", And @@ (EC[#[[1]], #[[2]]] . UnitVector[dC, 1] === ConstantArray[0, dC] & /@ {{1, 2}, {1, 3}, {2, 3}})},\n        {\"v1 . g0^-1 = (1 - k1 z1) e1^T exp((p1' - p1) E12)\", Simplify[v1C . Inverse[g0C] - (1 - k1 z[1]) UnitVector[dC, 1] . MatrixExp[(p1pC - p1) EC[1, 2]]] === ConstantArray[0, dC]},\n        {\"GT patterns (basis order)\", ps[{lamC}]},\n        {\"v_new (exact)\", Factor /@ vnewC}\n    },\n    Frame -> All, Alignment -> Left\n]",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [
