   "value": "(* ---- 5. Where the non-highest weights come from. With a diagonal twist t-hat commutes with the Cartan E_ii, so v1 (1 - k2 t-hat)\n   stays in the weights of e1^T e^{a E12}. Writing v_new = v1 g0^-1 (1 - k2 g0 t-hat g0^-1), the conjugation turns the twist into\n   G1 = g0 G g0^-1 (plain 3x3 matrix units; L1-mathcalA covariance), t^M_2 = sum_{I,J} qminor_{I,J} det M_{J,I} (quantum Cauchy-Binet).\n   G1 is upper triangular, its (1,3) entry vanishes because of the vacL relation for p3, and its off-diagonal entries are O(ε). ---- *)\nClearAll[qminGenC, tMC, g0plainC, G1C];\nqminGenC[II_, JJ_][x_] := Sum[Signature[s] Dot @@ Table[LaxC[II[[s[[k]]]], JJ[[k]]][x - (k - 1) h], {k, Length[II]}], {s, Permutations[Range[Length[II]]]}];\ntMC[M_][x_] := Sum[qminGenC[II, JJ][x] Det[M[[JJ, II]]], {II, Subsets[Range[3], {2}]}, {JJ, Subsets[Range[3], {2}]}];\ng0plainC = MatrixExp[p1 {{0, 1, 0}, {0, 0, 0}, {0, 0, 0}}] . MatrixExp[p2 {{0, 0, 1}, {0, 0, 0}, {0, 0, 0}}] . MatrixExp[p3C {{0, 0, 0}, {0, 0, 1}, {0, 0, 0}}];\nG1C = Simplify[g0plainC . DiagonalMatrix[z /@ Range[3]] . Inverse[g0plainC]];\nGrid[\n    {\n        {\"t-hat commutes with E11, E22, E33\", And @@ Table[Simplify[tHatC . EC[i, i] - EC[i, i] . tHatC] === ConstantArray[0, {dC, dC}], {i, 3}]},\n        {\"weights in the support of e1^T e^{a E12} t-hat\", Union[Table[If[Simplify[(UnitVector[dC, 1] . MatrixExp[a EC[1, 2]] . tHatC)[[n]]] =!= 0, wtC[[n]], Nothing], {n, dC}]]},\n        {\"Cauchy-Binet: t^G_2 from the general formula\", Simplify[tMC[DiagonalMatrix[z /@ Range[3]]][θ[1]] - tGC[2][θ[1]]] === ConstantArray[0, {dC, dC}]},\n        {\"covariance: g0 t^G_2 g0^-1 = t^{G1}_2\", Simplify[g0C . tGC[2][θ[1]] . Inverse[g0C] - tMC[G1C][θ[1]]] === ConstantArray[0, {dC, dC}]},\n        {\"G1 = g0 G g0^-1\", MatrixForm[G1C]},\n        {\"G1 at z = e^{φ ε}, O(ε)\", MatrixForm[Normal[Series[G1C /. z[k_] :> Exp[φ[k] ε], {ε, 0, 1}]]]}\n    },\n    Frame -> All, Alignment -> Left\n]",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [
    {
     "items": [
