  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "**Why the rule $\\nu_3\\le\\lambda_2$ (cell 14, exact).** Site 2 is $e_1^T$, so the site-1 weight satisfies $\\mu_3=\\nu_3$. Two mechanisms cap $\\mu_3$:\n\n- **(a) $\\hat t$ families** (old $v_{\\rm new}$, det $v'_{\\rm new}$). The rotation part $e_1^Te^{aE_{12}}$ has $\\mu_3=0$. Each $\\operatorname{qminor}_{I,J}$ is weight-homogeneous with $|I|=|J|$, so it moves at most one unit into slot 3, for **any** twist. Hence $\\mu_3\\le$ the number of insertions, which is $\\le\\lambda_2$. Exact check: for a general $3\\times3$ twist $M$, $e_1^Te^{aE_{12}}t^M_2(\\theta_1)\\equiv0$ at $(1,0,2)$ and $(0,1,2)$. So the zero $(1,3)$ entry of $G_1$ is **not** what limits these families.\n- **(b) $t_{\\{2,1\\}}(\\theta_1)$ family.** $G^{-1}g_0Gg_0^{-1}$ has zero $(1,3)$ entry (vacL relation), so it equals $e^{yE_{23}}e^{xE_{12}}$. Slot 3 is filled only by $E_{23}$ acting on row 2, and $e_1^TE_{23}^k=0$ for $k>\\lambda_2$.\n\n**Hypothetical fix.** $v^{(2)}=e_1^TG^{-2}g_0G^2g_0^{-1}$ has $(1,3)$ entry $-p_2(z_1-z_2)(z_1-z_3)/z_1^2=O(\\varepsilon^2)$. Its singlet overlap is $3p_2^2(z_1-z_2)^2(z_1-z_3)^2(z_1z_2+z_1z_3+z_2z_3)/(z_1^4z_2^2)\\ne0$, with $(0,1,2)$ leading order $9p_2^2\\varphi_{12}^2\\varphi_{13}^2\\,\\varepsilon^4$. Together with all the other families this gives **6/6**. It is **not** $\\langle\\mathrm{vacL}\\otimes\\mathrm{vacL}|t_{\\{2,1\\}}(\\theta_1)^2$: that covector has rank 4, so it is not on one site (`L2-localizing-transfer.wb` cell 8).",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "### The covector $v_{\\rm new}$ explicitly (finite twist, no untwisting limit)\n\nThis is the functional $\\langle k_1^{u/h}Q_1\\rangle\\langle k_2^{u/h}Q_{12}\\rangle$ with the site-2 rotation undone globally:\n$$\\big(\\langle v_{\\rm tot}|\\otimes\\langle\\mathrm{vacL}|\\big)\\,(g_0^{-1}\\otimes g_0^{-1})=\\langle v_{\\rm new}|\\otimes e_1^T,\\qquad \\langle v_{\\rm new}|=\\langle v_1|\\big(1-k_2\\,\\hat t(\\theta_1)\\big)\\,g_0^{-1}.$$\nThe values are `Factor /@ vnewC` from cell 3, exact. The basis is the GT basis of $[2,1,0]$ in the notebook's order, with patterns $\\{\\{m_{11}\\},\\{m_{12},m_{22}\\},\\{2,1,0\\}\\}$. The weight is $(E_{11},E_{22},E_{33})$. $p_3$ has been eliminated with the vacL relation $p_3=p_2(z_3-z_1)/(p_1(z_2-z_3))$.\n\n| # | GT pattern | weight | component of $v_{\\rm new}$ |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | $\\{2\\},\\{2,1\\}$ | $(2,1,0)$ | $\\tfrac12\\,(1-k_1z_1)(2-k_2z_1z_2)$ |\n| 2 | $\\{2\\},\\{2,0\\}$ | $(2,0,1)$ | $-\\dfrac{k_2p_2}{2p_1}\\,z_1(1-k_1z_1)(z_1-z_3)$ |\n| 3 | $\\{1\\},\\{2,1\\}$ | $(1,2,0)$ | $\\tfrac12\\,k_1p_1(z_1-z_2)(2-k_2z_1z_2)$ |\n| 4 | $\\{1\\},\\{2,0\\}$ | $(1,1,1)$ | $-\\tfrac12\\,k_2p_2\\,(2k_1z_1-1)(z_1-z_2)(z_1-z_3)$ |\n| 5 | $\\{1\\},\\{1,1\\}$ | $(1,1,1)$ | $-\\tfrac12\\,k_2p_2\\,(z_1-z_2)(z_1-z_3)$ |\n| 6 | $\\{1\\},\\{1,0\\}$ | $(1,0,2)$ | $0$ |\n| 7 | $\\{0\\},\\{2,0\\}$ | $(0,2,1)$ | $k_1k_2p_1p_2\\,(z_1-z_2)^2(z_1-z_3)$ |\n| 8 | $\\{0\\},\\{1,0\\}$ | $(0,1,2)$ | $0$ |\n\nAs one vector:\n$$\\langle v_{\\rm new}|=\\Big(\\tfrac12(1-k_1z_1)(2-k_2z_1z_2),\\ -\\tfrac{k_2p_2}{2p_1}z_1(1-k_1z_1)(z_1-z_3),\\ \\tfrac12k_1p_1(z_1-z_2)(2-k_2z_1z_2),\\ -\\tfrac12k_2p_2(2k_1z_1-1)(z_1-z_2)(z_1-z_3),\\ -\\tfrac12k_2p_2(z_1-z_2)(z_1-z_3),\\ 0,\\ k_1k_2p_1p_2(z_1-z_2)^2(z_1-z_3),\\ 0\\Big)$$\n\nNotes:\n- $\\theta_1$ and $h$ drop out exactly.\n- At $k_2=0$ it is $(1-k_1z_1)\\,e_1^Te^{aE_{12}}$ with $a=p_1k_1(z_1-z_2)/(1-k_1z_1)$, supported on components 1 and 3 only.\n- Every other component carries $k_2$. It comes from $\\hat t^{G_1}$ with $G_1=g_0Gg_0^{-1}$, whose off-diagonal entries supply the factors $(G_1)_{12}=p_1(z_2-z_1)$ and $(G_1)_{23}=p_2(z_1-z_3)/p_1$.\n- Components 6 and 8, the weights $(1,0,2)$ and $(0,1,2)$, vanish identically at finite twist. This is the $\\mu_3\\le\\lambda_2$ cap. Since component 8 is the only one that pairs with the singlet, $\\langle v_{\\rm new}\\otimes e_1^T|\\text{singlet}\\rangle=0$ exactly.\n- The octet components (4, 5) are in the ratio $(2k_1z_1-1):1$.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  }
 ],
